content.text:
Now main.js: orchestrate.

Imports Game, Renderer, UI, Sfx, config, art getSprites maybe. Game, Renderer, Sfx, UI.

Flow:
```
const canvas=...
const game=new Game();
const renderer=new Renderer(canvas, game);
const sfx=new Sfx();
let starting=false;
const hooks = {
 start(useSave) { if(starting) return; starting=true; if(useSave && game.load()) {...} else { game.reset(); } game.running=true; game.paused=false; game.speed=1; renderer.resetCamera(); renderer.pointer.inside=false; ui.hideStart(); ui.syncAll(); ui.startMessage(); saveTimer...; starting=false; },
 newGame() { game.clearSave(); game.reset(); game.running=true; game.paused=false; game.speed=1; renderer.resetCamera(); renderer.pointer.inside=false; ui.hideStart(); ui.hideWin(); ui.closeModal?? (modal handled); ui.syncAll(); ui.startMessage(); },
};
const ui = new UI(game, renderer, sfx, hooks);
```
But hooks reference `ui` before initialization (temporal dead zone). Define `let ui;` then hooks callbacks referencing ui at invocation (after assignment). Fine.

Game constructor resets and creates state; game.running false. UI syncAll. Start screen shows.

`start(useSave)`:
- If useSave && game.load() succeeds: keep state, game.running=true, etc.
- Else: game.reset() new.
- Clear toasts? syncAll clears.
- Set `renderer.resetCamera()` after state reset; terrain reset via reset event.
- `ui.hideStart()`.
- `ui.syncAll()`.
- `ui.startMessage()`.
- `game.running = true`, paused=false, speed=1.
- Start autosave loop? Use setInterval or in RAF accumulate.
- Maybe auto-save every 10s only when running and started.
- Need mark `started=true`.

`newGame()`:
- game.clearSave(); game.reset(); set running true; paused false; speed 1; renderer.resetCamera(); ui.hideStart(); ui.hideWin(); ui.syncAll(); ui.startMessage(); started=true; close modal if open (UI may call close itself). If called from confirm modal, closeModal then new. If from win "New Settlement", hideWin done.
- Start screen might be visible (if new clicked on start with no save) → hideStart.
- Toast "A new valley awaits." maybe startMessage.

Input:
- Pointer tracking with Map for multi-touch.
- Variables: pointers Map(pointerId→{x,y}), dragStart, dragging, lastPos, pinch.
- On pointerdown on canvas:
  - if start screen visible or modal/win? canvas covered by overlays (pointer events). HUD overlay pointer-events none except panels. Canvas still receives in gaps. If game not running → ignore.
  - capture pointer? canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId).
  - add pointer.
  - if one pointer: dragStart={x,y}, last={x,y}, moved=false.
  - if two: pinchStart distance and midpoint, pinchZoomStart.
- pointermove:
  - update renderer.pointer = {x,y,inside:true} always (for ghost/hover).
  - if pointers size 1 and pointer down: if distance from start > 5 → moved=true; if moved pan by delta (screen). update last.
  - if two pointers: compute distance ratio; zoom around midpoint; also pan by midpoint delta. Set moved=true.
- pointerup:
  - remove pointer.
  - if !moved and it was primary and pointers size 0:
    - handleClick(x,y)
  - if pointer count becomes 0 reset.
- pointerleave: renderer.pointer.inside=false (unless dragging?).
- pointercancel.
- wheel: preventDefault; zoom factor exp(-deltaY*0.0015) around cursor; set userZoomed via renderer.zoomAt.
- contextmenu: preventDefault; cancel placement.
- Use passive false for wheel.

handleClick(sx,sy):
- if game.placement:
  - set renderer.pointer to click position (for tile calc) — tileUnderPointer uses pointer. Set pointer x,y.
  - tile = renderer.tileUnderPointer(game.placement); if null return.
  - result = game.placeBuilding(type,tile.x,tile.y)
  - if ok: ui.afterPlace(); sfx already via game event. Maybe renderer pointer inside.
  - else ui.placementError(result.reason)
- else:
  - world = screenToWorld; building = renderer.buildingAt(world.x,world.y)
  - if building: ui.selectBuilding(id) else ui.clearSelection()
- No building hit → clear.

Add Renderer.buildingAt method. Implement now via edit.

Keyboard:
```
window.addEventListener('keydown', e=>{ if(ui.handleKey(e)) e.preventDefault? handleKey may prevent; });
```
handleKey already prevents for space. To avoid double, just call.
- Prevent browser zoom on Ctrl+wheel etc. wheel handler.

Resize:
- `window.addEventListener('resize', ()=>renderer.resize())`; also visualViewport? On mobile orientation change, setTimeout 50. Add.
- `window.addEventListener('orientationchange', ...)`.

Loop:
```
let last=performance.now();
function frame(now){
 const realDt=Math.min((now-last)/1000, 0.1); last=now;
 if (game.running && !game.paused && game.speed>0) game.update(realDt*game.speed);
 renderer.draw(realDt);
 ui.update(realDt);
 autosaveTimer += realDt;
 if (started && autosaveTimer>12) { autosaveTimer=0; game.save(); }
 requestAnimationFrame(frame);
}
```
Renderer particles use real dt even when paused; smoke continues. Good. But game.update with scaled dt: worker animations and timers speed up. Renderer animations normal speed; fine.
- When game.paused, renderer still draws smoke and water (nice). Particles update.
- On page hidden, pause? Add visibilitychange: if hidden and running, remember paused, set paused true? Could auto-pause to save; but autosave. Maybe set game.paused=true when hidden and restore? Simpler auto-save on visibility hidden.
- beforeunload save.
- Autosave only if started; save every 12s. `game.autoSave` optional used in finish/quest; assign `game.autoSave = () => { if(started) game.save(); }` to save immediately. But saving on every quest/build may be fine. Ensure not too frequent. We'll set.

- Save on pause? not needed.

Start:
- UI constructed with hooks. `started=false`.
- If game.hasSave(), start button Play loads. UI start note.

`startGame(useSave)`:
```
if (starting) return;
starting=true;
let loaded=false;
if(useSave) loaded=game.load();
if(!loaded){ game.reset(); }
game.running=true; game.paused=false; game.speed=1;
renderer.resetCamera();
ui.hideStart(); ui.syncAll(); ui.hideWin(); ui.closeModal? no modal.
started=true; starting=false;
ui.startMessage();
game.save();
```
- On load, `game.load` emits reset; UI syncAll before started maybe. Then syncAll again. Fine.
- If save was from won state, show win? Maybe not on continue; win flag true, quest complete. Keep playing. Fine.
- If loaded, toast welcome back. Start message uses hasSave() true still (save exists). Good.
- If no save and Play → game.reset; clearSave? existing save absent. fine.
- On start, if loaded save has game.running false (load sets false), set true.
- Camera center: after load maybe center on settlement? resetCamera centers map center; storehouse near center. Good.

`newGame()`:
```
game.clearSave();
game.reset();
game.running=true; game.paused=false; game.speed=1;
started=true;
renderer.resetCamera();
ui.hideStart(); ui.hideWin(); ui.syncAll(); ui.startMessage();
game.save();
```
- If called from win overlay, hideWin first (UI btnAgain already hides). fine.
- If from menu confirm, UI closes modal before calling. fine.

Autosave on reset? save immediately to preserve new state.

Building hit test add to Renderer:
```
buildingAt(wx,wy) {
 const list=[...game.buildings].sort((a,b)=>(b.y+b.h)-(a.y+a.h));
 for(const b of list){
  const top = b.y*TILE - (b.type==='townhall'?60:30);
  if(wx>=b.x*TILE-6 && wx<=(b.x+b.w)*TILE+6 && wy>=top && wy<=(b.y+b.h)*TILE+8) return b;
 }
 return null;
}
```
Roof extends up ~50px for 2x2; top = b.y*TILE - 24. Use -28 for 2x2, -62 townhall.

Also clicking building should not happen if clicking tree in front; okay.

Camera pan: Use drag threshold 5px; when dragging with one pointer, pan. When two fingers, pinch and pan. Implement pointer logic robustly.

Pseudo:

```
const pointers = new Map();
let drag = null; // {startX,startY,lastX,lastY,moved}
let pinch = null;

canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {
 if (!game.running) return;
 if (e.button !== undefined && e.button !== 0 && e.pointerType==='mouse') return;
 canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
 pointers.set(e.pointerId,{x:e.clientX,y:e.clientY});
 updatePointer(e);
 if(pointers.size===1){
   drag={startX:e.clientX,startY:e.clientY,lastX:e.clientX,lastY:e.clientY,moved:false,id:e.pointerId};
   pinch=null;
 } else if(pointers.size===2){
   drag=null;
   const [a,b]=[...pointers.values()];
   pinch={dist:Math.hypot(a.x-b.x,a.y-b.y), mid:{x:(a.x+b.x)/2,y:(a.y+b.y)/2}};
 }
});
```
Coordinates: canvas is full-screen at 0,0, so clientX/Y equals CSS canvas coords (no offset). Better compute rect and subtract to be safe. Use `const r=canvas.getBoundingClientRect(); x=e.clientX-r.left`.
- Store pointer positions in canvas coords.

pointermove:
```
if(!pointers.has(id)) { updatePointer(e); return; } // hover
update pointer map.
updatePointer.
if(pinch && pointers.size>=2){
  const [a,b]=...; const dist=...; const mid=...;
  if(pinch.dist>0) renderer.zoomAt(mid.x,mid.y, dist/pinch.dist);
  renderer.pan(mid.x-pinch.mid.x, mid.y-pinch.mid.y);
  pinch={dist,mid}; drag=null;
} else if(drag && drag.id===id){
  const dx = x-drag.lastX, dy = y-drag.lastY;
  if(!drag.moved && Math.hypot(x-drag.startX,y-drag.startY)>5) drag.moved=true;
  if(drag.moved) renderer.pan(dx,dy);
  drag.lastX=x; drag.lastY=y;
}
```
Note panning camera when dragging map: renderer.pan(dx,dy) subtracts, correct (drag right moves map right).
- Pinch zoomAt mid then pan by mid delta; order okay.

pointerup:
```
const p = pointers.get(id); pointers.delete(id);
if(drag && drag.id===id){
 const wasDrag=drag.moved;
 drag=null;
 if(!wasDrag) handleTap(p.x,p.y);
}
if(pointers.size<2) pinch=null;
if(pointers.size===1){ // re-init drag for remaining pointer
 const [pid,pos]=[...pointers.entries()][0]; drag={...}
}
```
- If tap was on UI? canvas only gets events when not over UI because UI pointer-events auto; but topbar etc. Good.
- For mouse, pointerup occurs on canvas captured; if user drags and releases outside, still fine.
- `pointerleave`: if no pointers down, pointer.inside=false. But with capture, pointerleave may fire; use if pointers.size===0.
- `pointerenter` update inside.
- contextmenu: cancel placement; prevent.

Tap placement uses last pointer p coordinates; set renderer.pointer {x:p.x,y:p.y,inside:true} before tile calc to ensure correct ghost location. Good.

Mouse hover: pointermove updates renderer.pointer for ghost. On touch, after tap pointer stays; ghost might remain at last tap. Fine.

On desktop, after placing, placement ends; pointer inside remains.

`updatePointer(e)`:
```
const r=canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
renderer.pointer.x=e.clientX-r.left; ...
renderer.pointer.inside=true;
```

Wheel:
```
e.preventDefault();
const r=...; renderer.zoomAt(x,y, Math.exp(-e.deltaY*0.0015));
```
Clamp factor per event maybe 0.8-1.25.

Keyboard: `window.addEventListener('keydown', e=>{ ui.handleKey(e); });`
- Prevent default for handled? UI calls preventDefault only for space. For digits, browser might trigger quick find? no. For +/- maybe. We can have handleKey return bool and main `if (handled) e.preventDefault()`. But UI already preventDefault for space/start. Main can also. Let's do:
```
if (ui.handleKey(e)) e.preventDefault();
```
- Avoid intercepting when modifier keys (ctrl/meta) to preserve shortcuts. In main: if (e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey||e.altKey) return. But 'm' with ctrl? skip. Good.

Prevent page scroll/gestures:
- CSS touch-action none on canvas; body overflow hidden.
- Add `gesturestart` preventDefault for iOS? `document.addEventListener('gesturestart', e=>e.preventDefault())` maybe. Add.
- Prevent double-tap zoom? viewport maximum-scale=1 and touch-action manipulation on buttons. Good.

Auto-save:
```
let saveClock=0;
in frame: if(started && game.running){ saveClock += realDt; if(saveClock>12){saveClock=0; game.save();}}
```
